      "notes": "The digit by digit approach relies on each digit being k / (n-1)! at that point.\nk gets recalculated at each iteration by doing k % (n-1)!\nMaintain an array of the numbers that haven't been used yet.\nThe calculations appear to be easier if k is deducted by 1 upfront (you then have 0 index block sizes).\nThis approach is O(n^2) time complexity (build the array and the array removal), O(n) space complexity",
